  "raw_label": "postponed_or_procedural",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Ashish Jaiswal vs State Of U.P. Thru. Prin. Secy. Excise ... on 31 August, 2024 Author: Sangeeta Chandra Bench: Sangeeta Chandra High Court Of Judicature At Allahabad, Lucknow Bench ?Neutral Citation No. - 2024:Ahc-Lko:59919-Db Court No. - 3 Case :- Writ - C No. - 7450 of 2024 Petitioner :- Ashish Jaiswal Respondent :- State Of U.P. Thru. Prin. Secy. Excise Deptt. Govt. Civil Sectt. Lko And 6 Counsel for Petitioner :- Lalji Yadav,Balram Yadav",
    "facts": "It is the case of the petitioner that the petitioner has applied for grant of a license for running a Ashish Jaiswal vs State Of U.P. Thru. Prin. Secy. Excise ... The Food Safety and Drugs Administration has also given a license to the petitioner but even after all formalities having been completed, the District Excise Officer is sitting tight over the matter, hence the present petition has been filed with the aforesaid prayer. 6. In pursuance of the Rules as amended from time to time, the Excise Commissioner, Prayagraj, has issued a circular on 05.07.2024 regarding a check list to be properly filled up for issuance of Bar License and in the said check list, at Serial No.4 mention has been made of the amended Rules 6(1)(J) of the Rules of 2020.",
    "arguments": "5. Learned counsel for the State respondents has produced a copy of the instructions sent by District Excise Officer, Pratapgarh dated 29.08.2024, which is kept on record, wherein it has been stated that under Rules 6 (1) (J) of the relevant Rules of U.P. Abkari Niyamawali, 2020, which states that a Bar License shall not be granted unless the premises is not situated within a district of 500 mts of the outer edge of a National or State Highway or of its service lane along the highway and the premises shall not be either visible or directly accessible from a National or State Highway. The proviso to the said Rule also states that in case of areas comprised in local bodies with a population of 20,000 or less, the distance shall be 220 metres."
  },
